Now I understand the `domain_to_punycode` bug. In the non-ASCII branch:

```c
labellen = outsize - outlen;
if (punycode_encode(inputlen, input, &labellen, out + outlen))
    return 1;
outlen += labellen;
```

`labellen` is set to `outsize - outlen` (the remaining space). But `punycode_encode` writes `labellen` bytes to `out + outlen`. If `labellen == outsize - outlen`, then it writes exactly up to `out[outsize-1]`, which is the last byte. But then `out[outlen] = 0` at the end writes the NUL terminator at `out[outsize]`, which is 1 byte past the buffer! That's the "write buffer overflow by 1".

The fix: `labellen = outsize - outlen - 1` to leave space for the trailing `\0`.

